# Copy this file to .env (gitignored; never commit it). The workshop server reads
# .env at start and keeps the key on the server; it never reaches the browser.
# In production the same names are set in the host's environment (fly secrets
# for the secret ones, fly.toml [env] for the rest); see docs/DEV_GUIDE.md §11.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional: the model behind the design agent (default claude-opus-5-5)
WORKSHOP_MODEL=
# Optional: the port the workshop server listens on (default 8787)
WORKSHOP_PORT=
# Optional: extra page origins allowed to call the server, comma-separated. Pages on
# http://localhost or http://127.0.0.1 (any port) are always allowed; every other
# Origin gets 403, so a stray tab cannot spend the key. In production: exactly the
# deployed origin, e.g. https://<app>.fly.dev
WORKSHOP_ORIGINS=
# Optional: extra Host header values the server answers to, comma-separated
# (localhost and 127.0.0.1 always; anything else is refused against DNS rebinding).
# In production: exactly the deployed host, e.g. <app>.fly.dev
WORKSHOP_HOSTS=
# The access code players type once (kept on their device). Unset: no code, and the
# server will only listen on a loopback address. Required before WORKSHOP_BIND can be
# anything else. Rotate it by setting a new value and restarting; players are asked again.
WORKSHOP_ACCESS_CODE=
# Model calls per UTC day, after which the workshop answers "closed for today" (default 50).
WORKSHOP_DAILY_CAP=
# A directory the day's count is kept in (a file written on every change), so a restart, a deploy
# or a machine stopped for idleness cannot start the day over. Unset: counted in memory. In
# production: the mounted volume (/data). The directory must exist.
WORKSHOP_STATE_DIR=
# The address to listen on (default 127.0.0.1). 0.0.0.0 in a container, only with an access code.
WORKSHOP_BIND=
# Serve the packed client from this directory as well (production: dist). Unset locally:
# any static server (python3 -m http.server -d dist 8000) serves the page.
WORKSHOP_STATIC=
# Heartbeat seconds while a request is in flight, so a proxy does not close a response that
# waits minutes for the model (default 0: plain responses). 20 in production.
WORKSHOP_KEEPALIVE_S=
# 1 when a trusted proxy sets X-Forwarded-For (Fly does): wrong access codes are then counted
# against the client's address rather than the proxy's.
WORKSHOP_TRUST_PROXY=
# Only when the page is hosted apart from the server: the server's public URL, read by
# `node pack.mjs` into the page and by the server into the page's connect-src. Unset when one
# process serves both (the page then uses its own origin).
WORKSHOP_URL=
